Mutation Lets Octopuses Make Proteins with Precision
---
Study from Nature: Certain species of shallow-water octopuses have a unique mutation that makes them extremely accurate protein builders. This mutation causes a break in an RNA strand in the core of the octopus's protein-making machinery.


